Show the label address with od --traditional -A n and a label.
With a label operand, each address is followed by the label address
in parentheses. When -A n suppresses the address, od switches to
format_address_paren to write only the parenthesized part, but that
function was given the plain address, while the label offset was
added only by format_address_label. So -A n with a label wrote the
real address in parentheses and the label had no effect. GNU od has
the same flaw. Add the label offset in format_address_paren, which
serves both cases.

---
 coreutils/od_bloaty.c |    6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/coreutils/od_bloaty.c
+++ b/coreutils/od_bloaty.c
@@ -879,12 +879,12 @@
 }
 
 #if ENABLE_LONG_OPTS
-/* only used with --traditional */
+/* only used with --traditional: the label address, in parentheses */
 static void
 format_address_paren(off_t address, char c)
 {
 	putchar('(');
-	format_address_std(address, ')');
+	format_address_std(address + G_pseudo_offset, ')');
 	if (c) putchar(c);
 }
 
@@ -892,7 +892,7 @@
 format_address_label(off_t address, char c)
 {
 	format_address_std(address, ' ');
-	format_address_paren(address + G_pseudo_offset, c);
+	format_address_paren(address, c);
 }
 #endif
 
